SkyPython terminal module

This module contains code from the terminal-emulator and terminal-view libraries of
the Termux project (https://github.com/termux/termux-app, tag v0.118.3), which are
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (see ../LICENSE). That code in turn
is based on Android-Terminal-Emulator by Jack Palevich
(https://github.com/jackpal/Android-Terminal-Emulator), also Apache License 2.0.

  src/main/java/com/termux/terminal/   terminal-emulator (screen model, VT/xterm parser)
  src/main/java/com/termux/view/       terminal-view (Android view, text selection)
  src/main/res/                        terminal-view resources
  src/test/java/com/termux/terminal/   terminal-emulator unit tests

Changes made for SkyPython:
  - JNI.java: no native code of its own; delegates to SkyPython's PTY library
    (dev.skyloft.skypython.runtime.Pty, runtime/src/main/cpp/pty.c, libskypty.so).
    The original jni/termux.c is not included.
  - TerminalSession.java: a failure to start the process is shown on the screen and
    reported through getStartError() instead of crashing; a finished session no longer
    resizes its closed (possibly reused) file descriptor.
All other files are unchanged.
